diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 1a55755..85bb5db 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,7 +6,25 @@ In-memory inventory service. `api.handle(request)` maps a request
 
 ## Endpoints
 
-- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...]}`: every item, ordered by `id`.
+- `GET /items` → `{"items": [...], "next_cursor": <string|null>}`: one page of
+  items, ordered by `id` ascending.
 - `GET /items/<id>` → the item, 404 when unknown, 400 when `id` is not a number.
 
+### `GET /items` query parameters
+
+- `limit` (optional): integer from 1 to 100, default 20.
+- `cursor` (optional): opaque string taken from a previous response's
+  `next_cursor`. Pass it back unchanged to fetch the following page.
+
+`next_cursor` is `null` on the last page. To read every item, request
+`/items`, then repeat with `cursor` set to each returned `next_cursor`
+until it is `null`.
+
+### Errors
+
+`GET /items` returns HTTP 400 with `{"error": "<message>"}` when `limit` is
+not an integer or is outside 1..100, or when `cursor` is malformed (not
+base64 of a decimal id). A well-formed cursor is accepted even if its item
+no longer exists: the page starts after that id.
+
 Run the tests with `python3 -m unittest`.
